                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment">      Ubuntu 11/04
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      There is an error in a TIFF image within a PDF document and when PDCcitt.getRGBImage() is called, there is a disparity between current PDFBox and v0.8.0. The issue is that there now TIFF decoding features whereas the older PDFBox used to hand that off to java.imageio. <br/>
<br/>
The bug here isn&#39;t in the Ccitt decoder, but rather in how PDCcitt.getRGBImage() handles an error. Rather than bombing out, I have reimplemented the old feature when an error is thrown.
  </td>
