</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment">      Using pdfbox1.6.0 on Windows 2003 server with java heap memory to 600 (which is maximum allowed), also tested with development environment windows Windows XP.
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      I am trying to load load bigger document using PDFReader component of PDFBox with version 1.6.0, if I have not set any maximum heap memory then load method invokes heap memory exception. On setting java max heap to 800 resolve the issue.<br/>
<br/>
But if I use the same PDFReader component of PDFBox with version 1.4.0 to load the same document with default java min and max heap memory it loads the pdf properly.<br/>
<br/>
Is it possible to to investigate why memory is leaked with pdfbox component version higher than 1.4.<br/>
<br/>
Thanks<br/>

  </td>
