                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment">      Fedora 13 Linux
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      Apparently a PDF is able to contain multiple files (like a Zip file); it&#39;s called<br/>
a PDF Package, described at<br/>
http://help.adobe.com/en_US/Reader/8.0/help.html?content=WSE034CA46-D08F-4fff-AA3C-FF04510DAEF0.html<br/>
<br/>
I have a simple example PDF Package, containing two sub-PDFs, but ExtractText<br/>
fails to extract their text.<br/>
<br/>
It does run successfully (no exceptions), but the text it extracts is just the boilerplate text<br/>
saying you should upgrade to Adobe Acrobat version 8 or later to view this PDF.<br/>

  </td>
