                <tr id="issuerow12555062" rel="12555062" data-issuekey="PDFBOX-1307" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    PDFBox
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="PDFBOX-1307" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/PDFBOX-1307">PDFBOX-1307</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                extracted images from a PDF sometimes come out inverted
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Minor
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">    <em>Unassigned</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Ian Holsman
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Ian Holsman
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 13/May/12 08:49 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 17/Mar/16 19:08 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 26/Feb/14 09:00 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        1.6.0            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        2.0.0            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        Rendering            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">4</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      Hi.<br/>
I am extracting images from a PDF (using the code below).<br/>
sometimes the images appear inverted<br/>
<br/>
    PDResources r = page.getResources();<br/>
        Map&lt;String, PDXObjectImage&gt; images = r.getImages();<br/>
        for (Map.Entry&lt;String, PDXObjectImage&gt; e : images.entrySet()) {<br/>
<br/>
            <br/>
            BufferedImage bi = null;<br/>
            try {<br/>
                bi = ((PDXObjectImage) e.getValue()).getRGBImage();<br/>
            } catch (Exception ee) {<br/>
                logger.info(&quot;can&#39;t read image ;-(&quot;, ee);<br/>
            }<br/>
<br/>
            if (bi != null) {<br/>
                currentPage.addImage(bi);<br/>
                ((PDXObjectImage) e.getValue()).write2file(&quot;/tmp/II&quot;+e.getKey());<br/>
            }<br/>
        }<br/>
       <br/>
and i&#39;m not sure, but there may be a memory leak grabbing the images this way as well.. but that could in my code.<br/>

  </td>
