                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment">      Windows XP
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      I have a PDF that when I read its contents using PDFBox some uppercase letters are being read as lowercase. For example :<br/>
- Word &quot;Testing&quot; is read as &quot;testing&quot;<br/>
- Word &quot;Eve&quot; is read as &quot;eve&quot;<br/>
- Word &quot;Deuteronomy&quot; is read as &quot;deuteronomy&quot;<br/>
<br/>
Andreas commented on this by: &quot;The pdf uses marked content to replace a string (14.9.4 Replacement Text of the PDF specs provides a simple example). And yes, PDFBox doesn&#39;t support it, yet.&quot;<br/>
<br/>
<br/>
Please check this 1-page sample PDF.
  </td>
