                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment">      PDFBox running in WebStart application
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      There is a huge performance impact while running PDFBox with Tika in a WebStart delopyed application.<br/>
<br/>
ResourceLoader.loadRessource() takes almost a third of processing time. It running stabdalone without WebStart, it performs quite fast. I am running JRE 1.7.0_07 on Win7 64bit environment.<br/>
<br/>
I don&#39;s know if this is a classpath scanning issue in WebStart or something else with PDFBox, so i file this as a bug.
