                                            <td class="issuelinks">                                        PDFBOX-1694                        </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      There&#39;s a bug in ASCII85OutputStream.java in <br/>
<br/>
     public final void write(byte[] b,int off, int sz)<br/>
<br/>
The effect of the bug is that buffers with length &lt; 3 produce no output. Fix:<br/>
<br/>
after <br/>
<br/>
     if(count &lt; 3) <br/>
     {<br/>
<br/>
add this line:<br/>
<br/>
         flushed = false;<br/>
<br/>
better: delete the whole function and let the superclass handle it. I doubt that the current implementation saves much time.
  </td>
