</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                                        PDFBOX-1769                        </td>
                                            <td class="environment">      Win 7
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      Attached PDFs result in &quot;1.0 Syntax error, Push back buffer is full&quot;, without any further output with the latest Preflight version. Older versions don&#39;t give this error, and provide more detailed miscellaneous output. I came across this while running Preflight on a dataset of 15,000 PDFs, and quite a number seem to be affected by this.<br/>
<br/>
Like https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/PDFBOX-1812, this is something that appears to have gone wrong quite recently (possibly commit r1549022 again?), as it used to work correctly in recent October commits.<br/>
<br/>
Again I included output files for both the current and the older (October) builds.
  </td>
