                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                                        PDFBOX-1730                        </td>
                                            <td class="environment">      XP, JDK7 45
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      The default imageType for PDFImageWriter.writeImage() is 8, which is TYPE_USHORT_565_RGB. I suggest to use TYPE_INT_RGB instead. The current default might create a poor user experience.<br/>
<br/>
I also suggest that the type and the resolution (&quot;screen resolution or 96 if not detected&quot;) be added to the javadoc.<br/>
<br/>
Finally, the variable &quot;imageType&quot; is used with two different meanings in that file: once as a string for the format, once as int for the BufferedImage type.
  </td>
