                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      The font descriptor flags are not set.<br/>
They are described in the document &quot;PDF reference 1.7&quot; at : 5.7.1 Font Descriptor Flags<br/>
<br/>
The methods in PDFontDescriptor are ready but never called :<br/>
setFlags()<br/>
setSerif()<br/>
setAllCap() which is used in a lot of PDF<br/>
...<br/>
<br/>
I saw some TODO that relate to that issue in the code, is it planned to be implemented soon?<br/>
<br/>
---<br/>
<br/>
UPDATE: This issue turned out to be caused by span tags and how Adobe Acrobat handles copy &amp; paste. Ultimately the PDF contains poor quality ToUnicode mappings and poor quality span tags, so there&#39;s no real fix.
