</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                Digital Signature information (parser bug?)
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Andreas Lehmkühler
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Nicolas Kaczmarski
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Nicolas Kaczmarski
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 26/Mar/14 09:16 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 13/Dec/14 14:14 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 18/Nov/14 10:34 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        1.8.7,                     2.0.0            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        1.8.8,                     2.0.0            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        Parsing            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">8</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      We have a signed PDF but signature is described without key &quot;Sig&quot;.<br/>
As you can see in the standard PDF 32000-1:2008 - Table 252 - Entries in a signature dictionary, this key is optional :<br/>
&quot;(Optional) The type of PDF object that this dictionary describes; if present, shall be Sig for a signature dictionary. &quot;<br/>
<br/>
But PDFBox seems to limit its research of signature only if this key &quot;Sig&quot; is present.<br/>
<br/>
What is your position about that?<br/>

  </td>
